  "body": "## Summary\n\nThis adds a finite complex-supplier construction for the U8 local word at base\n`abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf`.\n\nFour B-stage fragments of the form\n\n`x += a*s; y += q*x; x -= a*s`\n\nare replaced exactly by\n\n`y += q*x; y += (q*a)*s`.\n\nThe replacement preserves the complete rational linear map while removing one\nscalar operation from each fragment. No new kappa or selected-frontier change is\nclaimed.\n\n## Result\n\n- B-stage operations: **1,918 \u2192 1,914**\n- Scalar macros saved per orientation: **4**\n- Forward real-component primitive bound: **193,306 \u2192 193,254**\n- Backward real-component primitive bound: **193,354 \u2192 193,302**\n- Primitive saving per orientation: **52**\n- Exact arbitrary input columns checked: **728**\n- Paid rank profile: **unchanged**\n- Negative controls rejected: **9**\n\nThe four rewritten fragments begin at original B-stage indices 176, 194, 204,\nand 278.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe standalone verifier:\n\n- Pins the accepted `t37-replay.tar.gz` archive and canonical-word payload by\n  SHA-256.\n- Applies the four literal rewrites.\n- Compares the complete original and candidate B-stage maps using exact sparse\n  rational arithmetic.\n- Checks each three-register identity independently.\n- Reproduces the selected baseline receipts and primitive invoices.\n- Rejects four single-deletion controls, four incorrect-cross-term controls,\n  and one intervening-dependency control.\n- Regenerates and byte-compares the deterministic result certificate.\n\nThe unchanged local emitter and independent frame/wrapper auditor were also run\non the candidate. Both orientations retained the exact paid profile and\n192-bit allowance, with prefix bounds of 55 and 72 bits.\n\n## Reproduce\n\nPython 3.10+ and the standard library are sufficient:\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/u8-b-cancellation-seed32/verify.py\npython3 -I -B research/u8-b-cancellation-seed32/test_package.py\n```\n\nExpected output:\n\n```text\nPASS_U8_B_SHEAR_REWRITE_SEED32 rewrites=4 B=1918->1914 primitives=193306->193254/193354->193302 columns=728 controls=9 no_new_kappa\nPASS_U8_B_SHEAR_PACKAGE deterministic_result=1\n```\n\nNormal, optimized, and relocated executions passed. The selected-record checker,\nits five unit tests, and `git diff --check` also passed. No existing file or\nfile under `upstream/` is changed.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis establishes an exact finite B-stage identity and unchanged-emitter local\nadmission only. It does not rebuild:\n\n- The global owner map or whole-call hosting.\n- The complete complex-supplier invoice.\n- The outer 47-inequality assembly.\n- All-size/compiler or common-label realization.\n- Physical routing or mutable-source realization.\n- Precision/tape and exact-recovery interfaces.\n- Analytic transfer.\n\nConsequently, this PR claims neither a new kappa nor a practical multiplication\nspeedup. The finite replay is not a formal proof of the complete multiplication\ntheorem.\n\n## Provenance\n\n- Assignment seed: **32**\n- Track: **complex supplier**\n- Exact base: `abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf`\n- Source replay SHA-256:\n  `48285025105210b56a32d3d4d57a21b7591760acc709d38073e4dca339eb06fe`\n- Canonical word SHA-256:\n  `387a2266ffe006d20042221d967f67a4b18d9bb8de1cd1e01d4031b539fa74a5`\n\nThis builds on the selected U8 construction and retained complex-supplier\nlineage, including Jonathan Capalbo (#942), Chafik Boukhalfa (#890/#741),\nJeremy Kothe (#869/#870/#799), Hao Yan (#858), and the contributors credited\nby the inherited notices.\n\nPrepared for @martinxxx9 with substantial OpenAI assistance in research,\nmathematics, implementation, verification, and writing. No independent human\nreview is claimed. New material is Apache-2.0.\n",
